+# Full Data Export Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add a "╪ز╪╡╪»┘è╪▒ ╪د┘╪ذ┘è╪د┘╪د╪ز / Export Data" button to the smart analytics page (`╪د┘╪ز╪ص┘┘è┘ ╪د┘╪░┘â┘è`) and the comprehensive report page (`╪د┘╪ز┘é╪▒┘è╪▒ ╪د┘╪┤╪د┘à┘`) that downloads a single JSON file containing master data, indicator values, full smart analytics results, and (when cached) the comprehensive report text.
+
+**Architecture:** A new `app/engine/export.py` module builds the full package via `build_full_export(session, month, lang)`. A new `app/api/export.py` router exposes `GET /export/full-data?month=YYYY-MM|all&lang=ar|en` returning the JSON as a `StreamingResponse` attachment. Both pages call this one endpoint. Comprehensive report text comes ONLY from the persistent cache (`get_stored_report`) ظ¤ never AI-generated during export.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Python 3.14, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy (SQLite), pytest, dataclasses, numpy.
+
+**Established repo convention:** This project commits directly to `master` (all prior tasks did). No feature branch is created.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Reuse existing `analysis_cache` via `get_stored_report(session, month, lang)` from `app/engine/comparative/report_cache.py` for report text ظ¤ NEVER call `generate_comprehensive_report` or `_call_api` during export.
+- Smart analysis per month comes from `run_smart_analytics(session, month)` (in `app/engine/smart/__init__.py`).
+- JSON must be UTF-8, `ensure_ascii=False`, and numpy/NaN/Inf must be converted to native JSON types (never left as numpy scalars).
+- `month` param: `all` OR a `YYYY-MM` string. `lang` validated with `pattern="^(ar|en)$"`.
+- No data at all (no hospitals AND no indicator values) ظْ HTTP 404 with bilingual message.
+- A single month's analysis failure must not fail the whole export ظ¤ embed `{"error": str(e)}` in `analysis[month]` and continue.
+- All new tests go in `tests/test_export.py`.
+- Verify with: `python -m pytest tests/test_export.py -q` (all must pass) and `python -m pytest tests/test_comparative.py tests/test_smart_analytics.py -q` (existing tests must still pass).
+- Commit after each task with the exact message given.
+
